      "nets": ["/Microcontroller/HEATER", "Net-(D2-A)", "GND"],
      "observed": "The LED D2 is connected with its cathode (pin 1, K) on the active-high /Microcontroller/HEATER control net, while its anode (pin 2, A) is connected through R3 to GND.",
      "expected": "For a heater-on status LED driven from the active-high HEATER/GPIO1 net, the LED anode should be on /Microcontroller/HEATER and the cathode should return through R3 to GND, or the circuit should otherwise provide forward bias when GPIO1 is high.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"D2\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"K\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"D2\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"R3\") (pin \"2\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "A status LED (`D2`) and series resistor (`R3`) are also on the `HEATER` net"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "if average_temp < config.temperature { heater_output.set_high() }"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "D2 is reverse-biased when GPIO1/HEATER is high and has no forward drive path when it is low, so the intended heater-on indicator will not light. The heater control path itself remains electrically connected.",
      "confidence": 0.85
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The netlist shows D2 wired backwards for an active-high heater indicator: its cathode is on the HEATER control net and its anode is pulled to ground through R3, so the heater status LED will not illuminate as intended."
}

